GeomFill: a constrained filling's check that a boundary's tangent field
keeps its orientation leaves out the points where the field vanishes
(mitcad#1384). Example: a pocket's floor rounded with 0.8, twice the
radius of the concave 0.4 arcs at its corners: past each arc the walked
blend twists, and ChFi3d fills it with a three-sided
GeomFill_ConstrainedFilling whose fourth side is the point where the
floor's contact stands still. Along the two sides that run into that
point the Coons patch's tangent field comes to nothing (1e-15), and the
sign of its mixed product there was numerical noise. CheckTgte compares
every one of its 13 points with the first, so that noise decided whether
the patch's blending functions were made Law::MixBnd or left linear: at
one arc or the other, at 0.79999, 0.8 or 0.80001, on one body or a copy
0.0003 mm3 apart, the filled face came out one of two ways 0.04 mm apart
(1.146 or 1.204 mm2).

- CheckTgte takes the mixed products at its 13 points first and compares
  only those above 1e-9 of the largest along the boundary: a field that
  vanishes at a corner does not count as turning there.
